WHEN TO CALL
- Tool/build/test failure with actionable signal
- Repeated empty / irrelevant search result (=2 attempts)
- Discovered requirement or API/spec deviation
- Architectural or scope decision made
- Performance/regression concern detected
- Blocking assumption proven false

DO NOT CALL FOR
- Routine progress (use update_plan_progress)
- Re-describing plan steps
- Speculation without evidence
- General narration / brainstorming

INPUT (single field)
observation: Prefer a tag + evidence. Format:
<ERROR|DECISION|DISCOVERY|RISK|ASSUMPTION|PERF>: <concise fact> - <minimal action/result if any>
If you omit a tag, still include exact error codes, test names, or commands when available.

EXAMPLES
ERROR: Build failed CS0246 in FooService.cs: missing using for System.Linq
ERROR: Test failed MyTest.ShouldWork - assertion mismatch
DECISION: Use existing JsonConfigLoader instead of adding new parser
DISCOVERY: API /v2/items returns 404 for archived ids; adjust fallback logic
ASSUMPTION: Original step expects ModuleA init before ModuleB (reverse is required)

