<file path="docs/superpowers/plans/pushnotifications.md">
# PWA Push Notification System Implementation Plan

## Goal

Implement a reliable push notification system for the PWA using:

* ASP.NET Core API
* Azure App Service
* SQL Server
* Dapper
* ASP.NET Core HostedService background worker
* Web Push notifications (VAPID)

The system must support:

* Job Assigned To Me
* Job Ready For Review
* Job Denied
* Job Completed

The system must provide:

* Reliable delivery attempts
* Retry handling
* Error handling
* Structured logging
* Multiple devices per user
* Invalid subscription cleanup
* Idempotent processing
* Future extensibility for additional notification types
* Danish user-facing notification text

The API must never send push notifications directly. Notifications must always be queued and processed asynchronously.

---

# Architecture

```text
Business Event
      |
      ▼
Notification Service
      |
      ▼
Notification Queue (SQL)
      |
      ▼
PushNotificationWorker
      |
      ▼
Web Push Provider
      |
      ▼
User Device / PWA
```

The flow:

1. User action occurs.
2. Business logic completes the database operation.
3. Notification request is inserted into the queue.
4. HostedService processes pending notifications.
5. Push notification is delivered to registered user devices.
6. Delivery result is logged.

---

# Components

## API

Responsibilities:

* Manage push subscriptions.
* Create notification queue entries.
* Trigger notifications from business events.

The API must not:

* Call Web Push directly.
* Wait for notification delivery.
* Handle retries.

---

## Notification Service

Create:

```csharp
INotificationService
NotificationService
```

Responsibilities:

* Create notification payloads.
* Create localized Danish messages.
* Insert notification queue records.
* Handle notification templates.

Example:

```csharp
await notificationService.QueueJobAssigned(
    userId,
    jobId,
    jobNumber,
    customerAddress);
```

---

## Hosted Service

Create:

```csharp
PushNotificationWorker : BackgroundService
```

Responsibilities:

* Poll notification queue.
* Claim pending notifications.
* Send push notifications.
* Handle retries.
* Log delivery.
* Remove invalid subscriptions.

---

# Database Design

## PushSubscriptions

Stores one record per user device.

```sql
CREATE TABLE PushSubscriptions
(
    Id UNIQUEIDENTIFIER PRIMARY KEY,

    UserId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER NOT NULL,

    Endpoint NVARCHAR(MAX) NOT NULL,

    P256Dh NVARCHAR(MAX) NOT NULL,

    Auth NVARCHAR(MAX) NOT NULL,

    UserAgent NVARCHAR(500),

    IsActive BIT NOT NULL DEFAULT(1),

    CreatedUtc DATETIME2 NOT NULL,

    LastSeenUtc DATETIME2 NOT NULL
)
```

A user can have multiple subscriptions:

```
User
 |
 ├── Phone
 ├── Laptop
 └── Tablet
```

---

## NotificationQueue

Stores notification requests.

```sql
CREATE TABLE NotificationQueue
(
    Id UNIQUEIDENTIFIER PRIMARY KEY,

    UserId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER NOT NULL,

    NotificationType NVARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,

    PayloadJson NVARCHAR(MAX) NOT NULL,

    Status NVARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,

    RetryCount INT NOT NULL DEFAULT(0),

    CreatedUtc DATETIME2 NOT NULL,

    ProcessingStartedUtc DATETIME2 NULL,

    NextAttemptUtc DATETIME2 NOT NULL,

    CompletedUtc DATETIME2 NULL,

    LastError NVARCHAR(MAX) NULL
)
```

Statuses:

```
Pending
Processing
Completed
Failed
```

---

## NotificationDeliveryLog

Tracks every delivery attempt.

```sql
CREATE TABLE NotificationDeliveryLog
(
    Id UNIQUEIDENTIFIER PRIMARY KEY,

    NotificationId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER NOT NULL,

    SubscriptionId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER NOT NULL,

    Success BIT NOT NULL,

    SentUtc DATETIME2 NOT NULL,

    ErrorMessage NVARCHAR(MAX)
)
```

---

# Notification Types

Create:

```csharp
public enum NotificationType
{
    JobAssigned,
    JobReadyForReview,
    JobDenied,
    JobCompleted
}
```

---

# Notification Payload

The payload must contain enough information to generate the user-facing message.

Example:

```json
{
  "jobId": "guid",
  "jobNumber": "12345",
  "customerAddress": "Søndergade 12, 8000 Aarhus C",
  "notificationType": "JobAssigned"
}
```

The worker should not depend on live database lookups to create notification text.

---

# User Facing Language Requirements

All notification text must be written in Danish.

The notification service is responsible for generating the final Danish title and body.

Do not place notification text inside controllers or business logic.

---

# Notification Templates

## Job Assigned

Purpose:

Inform the user that a new job has been assigned.

Required information:

* Job number
* Customer address

Title:

```
Nyt job tildelt
```

Body:

```
Job #12345 er tildelt dig.
Adresse: Søndergade 12, 8000 Aarhus C
```

---

## Job Ready For Review

Title:

```
Job klar til gennemgang
```

Body:

```
Job #12345 er klar til din gennemgang.
Adresse: Søndergade 12, 8000 Aarhus C
```

---

## Job Denied

Title:

```
Job afvist
```

Body:

```
Job #12345 er blevet afvist og kræver ændringer.
Adresse: Søndergade 12, 8000 Aarhus C
```

---

## Job Completed

Title:

```
Job afsluttet
```

Body:

```
Job #12345 er afsluttet.
Adresse: Søndergade 12, 8000 Aarhus C
```

---

# Push Delivery

Use:

```
WebPush.Net
```

Create:

```csharp
IPushSender
WebPushSender
```

Responsibilities:

* Build Web Push request.
* Send notification.
* Return success/failure.
* Handle provider errors.

---

# PWA Service Worker

Implement:

```
service-worker.js
```

Handle:

* push event
* notificationclick event

Example notification:

```javascript
self.registration.showNotification(
    "Nyt job tildelt",
    {
        body: "Job #12345 er tildelt dig.",
        icon: "/icons/icon-192.png",
        badge: "/icons/badge.png",
        tag: "job-12345",
        data:
        {
            url: "/jobs/12345"
        }
    }
);
```

---

# Notification Appearance

The operating system controls:

* Layout
* Fonts
* Colors
* Position
* Animation

The application can control:

* Title
* Body
* Icon
* Badge
* Image (where supported)
* Actions
* Tag
* Deep link

---

# Notification Click Handling

When a user clicks a notification:

1. Close notification.
2. Check if application window already exists.
3. Focus existing window if possible.
4. Otherwise open a new window.
5. Navigate to the relevant job.

Example:

```
/jobs/{jobId}
```

---

# Retry Strategy

Maximum retries:

```
5 attempts
```

Schedule:

```
Attempt 1:
Immediate

Attempt 2:
+1 minute

Attempt 3:
+5 minutes

Attempt 4:
+15 minutes

Attempt 5:
+1 hour
```

After final failure:

```
Status = Failed
```

---

# Error Handling

Handle:

## Temporary failures

Examples:

* Network failure
* Provider timeout
* Temporary service outage

Action:

* Retry.
* Log warning.
* Increment retry count.

---

## Permanent failures

Examples:

```
404
410 Gone
```

Meaning:

The subscription no longer exists.

Action:

* Disable subscription.
* Do not retry.

---

# Queue Processing

The worker must process notifications in batches.

Example:

```
50 notifications per cycle
```

Processing:

```
Find Pending
       |
       ▼
Claim rows
       |
       ▼
Send notifications
       |
       ▼
Update status
```

---

# Prevent Duplicate Processing

The system must support multiple application instances.

Notification claiming must be atomic.

Example:

```
Pending
   |
   ▼
Processing
```

Only one worker can claim a notification.

Use SQL transactions and row locking.

---

# Logging Requirements

Use structured logging.

Every log entry should include:

```
NotificationId
UserId
NotificationType
JobId
```

---

## Successful Delivery

Example:

```csharp
logger.LogInformation(
"Push notification sent. NotificationId={NotificationId}");
```

---

## Retry

Example:

```csharp
logger.LogWarning(
"Push notification failed. RetryCount={RetryCount}");
```

---

## Permanent Failure

Example:

```csharp
logger.LogError(
exception,
"Notification permanently failed");
```

---

# Invalid Subscription Cleanup

When delivery returns:

```
404
410 Gone
```

Update:

```
PushSubscriptions.IsActive = false
```

Do not retry.

---

# Localization Structure

Design for future languages:

```
NotificationService

 ├── DanishTemplates

 ├── EnglishTemplates (future)

 └── Other languages (future)
```

---

# Configuration

Store VAPID configuration:

```
PublicKey
PrivateKey
Subject
```

Rules:

* Private key only exists on backend.
* Never expose private key to PWA.
* Use Azure Key Vault for production secrets.

---

# Success Criteria

The implementation is complete when:

✅ Users can register push subscriptions.

✅ Multiple devices per user are supported.

✅ Job Assigned notifications work.

✅ Job Ready For Review notifications work.

✅ Job Denied notifications work.

✅ Job Completed notifications work.

✅ All user-facing messages are Danish.

✅ Job Assigned contains job number and customer address.

✅ Failed deliveries retry automatically.

✅ Invalid subscriptions are cleaned up.

✅ Every delivery attempt is logged.

✅ Duplicate processing is prevented.

✅ API requests are never blocked by push delivery.

✅ HostedService survives application restarts safely.

✅ Future notification types can be added without changing existing architecture.
</file>

